$O$ is the centre of the base and $M$ is the midpoint of edge $AD$.
Which side of right-angled triangle $TOM$ is the hypotenuse?

questions.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (M) at (3,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.2);
\draw (O)--(M)--(T)--cycle;
\draw (0.28,0)--(0.28,0.28)--(0,0.28);
\node[below] at (0,0) {$O$};
\node[below right] at (3,0) {$M$};
\node[above left] at (0,2.2) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The right angle is at $O$, so the hypotenuse is opposite it.
The hypotenuse is $TM$.

